course: dictionary
lesson: 1034
title: Booster: a helping push
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A booster is something that gives extra help, so that something works better, safer or stronger. The words around it tell you which kind of booster it is. «A child uses a booster seat until the adult belt fits, usually around 145 to 150 cm or 4 feet 9 inches tall.» The sentence is about seat belts and height, so a booster here is a raised seat that lifts a child up.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «The nurse said Sam needed a booster jab to stay protected.» Here a booster is an extra dose of a medicine. «In December 2015 a SpaceX Falcon 9 booster landed upright back on Earth after a launch to orbit.» Now a booster is a rocket part that gives extra push at launch.
explain: Use the test from earlier: swap your meaning into the sentence. «The good news was a confidence booster for the team.» Try "something that made the team feel more sure of themselves". It fits, so you have found the meaning. Ask yourself: what does this booster add or improve?
fact: A booster is something that gives extra help or lifts something up.
fact: A booster seat is a raised seat that lifts a child so the adult seat belt fits safely.
fact: A booster jab is an extra dose of a vaccine that keeps a person protected for longer.
fact: A rocket booster gives extra push at the start of a launch.
fact: Anything that increases or improves something can be called a booster, like «a confidence booster» or «a mood booster».
exercise: «Adult belts are made for adult bodies, so a child uses a booster seat until the belt fits.» What is a booster seat? | A soft pillow for sleeping in the back | A kind of car horn | *A raised seat that lifts a child up so the belt fits
exercise: «The nurse said Sam needed a booster jab to stay protected.» Why does Sam need a booster jab? | *To keep a vaccine working for longer | To make his arm grow bigger | To get a day off school | To stay protected for longer
exercise: «The good news was a confidence booster for the team.» What is a confidence booster? | *Something that makes the team feel more sure of themselves | Something that makes the team tired | A ball kicked high into the air
test: «In December 2015 a SpaceX Falcon 9 booster landed upright back on Earth after a launch to orbit.» In this sentence, booster means: | A kind of spelling test | A car seat for babies | *A rocket part that gives extra push at launch | A type of tent for camping
test: Which of these is a booster jab? | A plaster for a cut knee | A type of car seat | A sharp pain you feel when you are ill | *An extra dose of a vaccine that keeps you protected
exam: Which sentence uses booster to mean something that improves a feeling? | *«The sunny weather was a mood booster for the whole class.» | «The booster seat was in the back of the car.» | «The nurse gave me a booster jab.» | «The rocket booster fell into the sea.»
